00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.799
Thank you for the warm intro.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.490
All right, lot of things
I wanna cover today.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.310
Feel free to sit down,
unless you wanna stand.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.143
You do you.

00:01:15.269 --> 00:01:18.280
You know, I flew from
Malaysia this morning,

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.600
and I was thinking about
what I wanted to speak about,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.073
with this incredible crowd,

00:01:23.073 --> 00:01:24.970
and there was a lot of different things

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.170
running through my mind.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.750
But I broke them down
into a couple places.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:34.750
I think one of the things
that I'm very fearful of,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.510
is hypocrisy.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.720
I think it really sucks when people talk

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.140
out of both sides of their mouth,

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.120
and I think one of the things,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.680
that when I was growing
up in the business world

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.980
that became apparent to me,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.980
is why do people take
advice from individuals

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.900
who've never done something?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.733
Right?

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:57.726
I've spent a lot of time
thinking about that.

00:01:57.726 --> 00:02:00.890
Now, it's a very interesting
thing in my mind,

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.320
because I used to be very 100% about this,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.260
which is don't listen to anybody
who's never done something.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.500
But then I realized that
some of the best coaches

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.500
in sports history never played the game,

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.810
but understood how to give advice.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.312
So that kind of took a step back.

00:02:16.312 --> 00:02:18.160
But the thing that I've realized,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.960
was the reason that my initial reaction

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.550
was don't listen to anybody
who's never done it,

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.640
was that for me, when I communicate,

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.210
I'm incapable of being the kind of coach

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.500
for a football team if I never played it.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.250
I would never be good at that.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:42.164
Had I played baseball,
or football, or Jai-Alai

00:02:42.164 --> 00:02:44.340
or whatever it may be,

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.170
I would have then been
able to give advice.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.720
But if not, I couldn't watch film

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.650
or study the game and give advice.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.630
Going through this self-awareness
over the last 20 years,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.260
has allowed me to think

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.700
about why, over the
last two or three years,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.060
my content continues to
resonate even more than ever,

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.760
it's because I'm getting even more narrow

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.320
in what I talk about.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.860
One of my favorite comments
on my YouTube channel

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.810
or my podcasts or my
Instagram or LinkedIn,

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.740
is when somebody says Gary
V, you're getting boring.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.519
You say the same shit.

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:22.940
(audience laughing)

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.143
I go, that's the point.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.850
If you really understand the process,

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.190
I think there's way too many people

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.310
talking about stuff they don't understand

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.750
or, because they think
it will do well for them.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.280
I only wanna talk about the
stuff that I understand,

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.220
'cause it's the only way
I can bring any value.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.680
And I'm fine if somebody
feels like they got it.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.600
I think, how many people
here have watched my vlog?

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.190
Raise your hand.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.023
Thank you.

00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:53.990
So I think you guys know, on the vlog,

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.410
every 20, 30 episodes, 50 episodes,

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:57.730
I get weird and look at the camera

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.099
and say what the fuck are
you still watching this for?

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:01.610
(audience laughing)

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.730
And I think, when I think of myself,

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.020
in the personalities
that speak or write books

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.020
or put content, I feel
like I'm the reverse.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:14.020
I want people to hear me for free,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.120
and then go on and do their thing and win,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.840
instead of keeping people in my funnel

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.254
and monetize them through
courses or masterminds

00:04:22.254 --> 00:04:24.740
or other things.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.300
I think that's important,
and I'll tell you why.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.020
I think that it's super important

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:33.750
to watch who you take advice from.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.630
I always am fascinated
when people are like,

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.950
Gary, I've been watching
your business videos,

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.170
like a friend, forget about,

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.770
you know, somebody I've
known for 25 years.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.890
They're like Gary, I've been
watching your stuff lately,

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.320
but, my uncle tells me I should do this.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.940
And the first question I always ask is,

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.940
and the person's asking
a business question,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:54.500
and I ask them, well
tell me about your uncle.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.780
And they're like, well he's a gym teacher

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:58.660
at our high school.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:01.890
I'm like well, if you
want to be a gym teacher,

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:05.110
your uncle is a tremendous
person to listen to,

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.480
but if you wanna build a business,

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.450
I think I'm better at building
businesses than your uncle.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:14.360
And so, the reason I
start this talk this way

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.400
is 'cause I think I have a
little bit or a curve ball

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.440
for people that have been
following me for a little while.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.220
I think a lot of your know
that one of the things

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.000
I fear the most, fear,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.717
is I don't want to be
a motivational speaker.

00:05:24.717 --> 00:05:26.220
I don't like that at all.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.650
I mean it, I don't like it at all,

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.200
because I don't think of myself that way.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.572
But over the last year and a half,

00:05:31.572 --> 00:05:35.950
the reason I put out content
that may be more rah-rah

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.490
or things of that nature,

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.682
is 'cause I've realized, my god,

00:05:39.682 --> 00:05:42.170
my greatest strength,

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.160
the thing that I realize
I can give best advice on,

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.110
is I'm the byproduct
of very good parenting,

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.310
very good environment,

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.250
which means I didn't grow up with much,

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.190
so I'm not entitled,

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:59.340
very tried and true 20 years
of business, at this point,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.040
based on work ethic

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.410
and based on giving value to the customer

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.720
over anything else.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.060
And I realized that if you're
here on a beautiful Saturday

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.730
in the summer for this
talk, that we have to start

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.550
in the strategy of where your head's at,

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.895
and then I can talk to you about the fact,

00:06:19.895 --> 00:06:22.400
and this is just true, there's a reason,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.420
I don't know if you guys know this,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.370
but VaynerMedia is opening
an office in Singapore

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.692
in the first quarter of next year, right?

00:06:29.692 --> 00:06:31.570
(audience cheering)

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.710
So, I'm gonna be here a
lot more going forward

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:35.710
over the next five years.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:38.700
So if you see me in a restaurant,

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.373
don't just stare at me,
come over and say hello.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.667
But, I think that the
thing that's on my mind

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.630
in this market is mindset.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.380
I can give you the reasons

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.040
we're opening an office in Singapore,

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.080
because in southeast Asia,
my marketing strategies

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.870
of buying Facebook ads,
running ads with KOLs,

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.160
and giving them as much money as possible,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.480
doing podcast and LinkedIn content,

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:16.480
works better in Singapore
and Malaysia and Indonesia

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.280
than it does in America or Europe.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.810
So, all the propaganda that I push

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.630
around Facebook advertising
and Instagram and all that,

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:29.350
I promise you, whether you're a lawyer,

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.464
or you have an app startup,
or you wanna sell t-shirts,

00:07:33.464 --> 00:07:37.450
I don't understand why anyone's confused.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.710
The only practical advice
I have for you right now,

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.630
practical, black and white,

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:46.223
is run more ads on social media.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.600
And, if you're going to run
more ads on social media

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.010
to do whatever you're trying to sell,

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.080
your course, your
sneakers, your real estate,

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.073
whatever you do,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.340
there's one part that
breaks in running more ads

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:02.450
on social media,

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:05.960
do you know how to put
a good picture or video

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.090
or written word in the ad?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:13.650
The variable of running great
ads, is the creative itself.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:17.110
And I think too many people
don't respect the art enough,

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.770
they just respect the math.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:20.900
But from a practical standpoint,

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.093
everybody here should be
running a lot more social media.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.420
Nobody here is taking it serious enough.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.510
I'll tell you why.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:31.800
I take it more serious
than my own religion,

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.270
and I don't take it serious enough.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:37.420
So, if I'm up here and I
don't take it serious enough,

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.210
there is nobody here that is taking

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:43.700
how big of an opportunity
this is, serious enough.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.890
I will go back to tactics in a minute,

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.200
but let me tell you why I started my talk

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.450
on what am I best at?

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.200
And that should be my advice.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.300
What I'm best at is knowing
that the far majority

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.520
of people in this room right now,

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.460
have not achieved the success

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.330
or happiness they're looking for,

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.420
mainly on the back of the fact

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.263
that they value their mother
or father's opinion too much.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.170
The thing that I understand about life

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.550
and then that matters in business,

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.420
is you either listen to your own voice,

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.473
or you listen to somebody else's.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.600
The thing that people need to
understand more than anything,

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:29.600
is what is driving their ambition?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.770
Why are you doing what you're doing?

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:37.000
What are you trying to scratch?

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.030
What itch are you trying to scratch?

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.790
Are you trying to be successful

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.700
to prove to people that said you wouldn't?

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.660
Are you trying to be successful

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.790
because you love the process?

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:51.010
Are you doing it because you
wanna buy something fancy

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.990
to show people that you're successful?

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.710
Why do you do what you're doing?

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.733
And most of all, for who?

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.070
What happened to me,
through very good parenting,

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.823
is I played for myself.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:07.370
How many people say Rocky IV?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.920
The one in Russia, raise your hands,

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.030
I wanna just get a sense.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.140
Raise it high if you saw that movie.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:13.080
Good, good amount.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.902
In Rocky IV, he fights
a Russian guy, Rocky.

00:10:16.902 --> 00:10:21.740
The Russian guy talks about the pressure

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:25.130
of the whole Soviet Union
wanting him to beat Rocky,

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.050
and at one point he cracks,

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:30.480
and tells the Russian
government and all the fans,

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.083
fuck you, I'm not fighting
for you, I'm fighting for me.

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.950
I've always thought about
that scene my whole life,

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.990
and I didn't know why until
about two or three years ago,

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:46.990
which I realized oh my
god, I'm living for me.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.500
I'm playing this game for me.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.900
Not for anybody else.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:54.715
And everybody else is
playing for somebody else.

00:10:54.715 --> 00:10:57.880
And that was unbelievably liberating,

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.500
and I'll be very honest with you,

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.420
I was very grateful for that.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.190
I think a lot of people in this room

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.470
have to go home tonight and ask themselves

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.720
who they're playing for?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.674
Making your parents proud

00:11:11.674 --> 00:11:14.933
is usually the first step to disaster.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:17.830
I mean it.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.900
I understand that it's a interesting angle

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.030
to talk about this,

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.100
it's great to want to
make your parents proud,

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.063
but not at the expense of your happiness.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.080
And so, I've become
unbelievably fascinated

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.710
with the mindset of why people do stuff,

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:38.130
and why am I able to work 17 hours a day?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.670
I'm able to work 17 hours
a day 'cause I love it.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:44.560
Nobody works 17 hours a day
'cause of any other thing

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.023
because they love it.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.970
All the people that try to
teach you how to get rich

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.520
with the least amount of
work, they love the money.

00:11:54.631 --> 00:11:56.320
They love the money.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.670
People love the money.

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:01.170
A lot of people here are
here to figure out the secret

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.470
for the money.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.320
You love the money, you value the money.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.240
I don't value the money, I value the game.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.850
My game is how good am I at this?

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.853
I value the admiration.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.880
I value the admiration.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.260
That's a tough thing to say a little bit,

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.580
'cause it seems kinda
shallow, but it's my truth.

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:25.050
I was so over loved by my mother,

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.390
that when I went into the real world,

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.620
I still wanted the love.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:33.400
And I basically manifested
with my DNA and my environment

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.460
in a way that I,

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.370
there's only one reason
that I'm giving you

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.860
more value than most people,

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.230
it's because I want your admiration.

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.350
And the only way to get real admiration,

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.691
is to give the most.

00:12:46.691 --> 00:12:48.520
Simple as that.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.260
It's not super complicated.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:52.580
So I'm spending a lot of time

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.633
trying to figure out
what the fuck am I doing?

00:12:54.633 --> 00:12:57.723
What the fuck am I doing in
Singapore on Saturday right now?

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:03.320
